<figure class="research-figure operations-diagram">
  <div class="research-figure__header">
    <span class="figure-kicker">Three operations</span>
    <strong>One activation, three different questions</strong>
  </div>

  <div class="activation-source">
    <span>Shared input</span>
    <strong>Residual activation</strong>
    <code>h_l,t</code>
  </div>
  <div class="branch-rail" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>

  <div class="operation-lanes">
    <section>
      <header><span>01 · Observe</span><strong>Ranked readout</strong></header>
      <div class="operation-step">
        <small>Operation</small>
        <code>score every J-lens vector</code>
      </div>
      <div class="operation-result">
        <small>Answers</small>
        <strong>Which tokens rank highly?</strong>
        <p><code>spider</code>, <code>web</code>, <code>eight</code></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <header><span>02 · Approximate</span><strong>Sparse decomposition</strong></header>
      <div class="operation-step">
        <small>Operation</small>
        <code>gradient pursuit, a_i ≥ 0</code>
      </div>
      <div class="operation-result">
        <small>Answers</small>
        <strong>Which few directions reconstruct h?</strong>
        <p><code>h ≈ Σ a_i v_i</code>, with at most <code>k</code> active vectors</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <header><span>03 · Test</span><strong>Intervention</strong></header>
      <div class="operation-step">
        <small>Operation</small>
        <code>steer · ablate · swap</code>
      </div>
      <div class="operation-result">
        <small>Answers</small>
        <strong>Does changing it alter behavior?</strong>
        <p>Compare the clean and modified continuations.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <figcaption>
    Readout is observational, decomposition is a sparse reconstruction, and
    intervention is a causal test. A token appearing in the first result does
    not by itself establish either of the other two.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

